## Current phase

Phase 1.5 completes Beacon's engineering agent platform before major business-domain or UI expansion. The product implementation remains the Phase 1 marketing and lead-capture surface; Phase 1.5 changes the engineering factory used to build future work, not the product's deployed business scope.

No CRM, customer portal, project dashboard, billing surface, database, durable queue, or automation worker is authorized by this phase. The current in-memory orchestration simulation must not be presented or expanded as a live business runtime.

## Verified implementation baseline

The repository builds a static Astro marketing site, a Markdoc documentation site, a simulated workspace, and a narrow Cloudflare Worker contact handler.

Repository-native secure delivery definitions now include PR policy, quality, security, browser gates, immutable Action pins, artifact digest promotion, manual environment-gated deploy workflows, security policies, and operating runbooks. Unit tests cover the hardened contact boundary.

GitHub ruleset `Protect main` is active on the default branch. It blocks deletion and non-fast-forward updates, requires pull requests with resolved review conversations, requires signed commits and CodeQL, and grants no bypass. Six existing status contexts are required, but the new agent-platform check is not yet in the ruleset.

Preview, staging, and production GitHub environments exist. Production has no required reviewer and permits administrator bypass, so it is not the non-bypassable external gate required by Phase 1.5. The agent-evals environment, live provider evidence, deployment verification, and rollback drill also remain pending. No deployment was performed as part of this implementation.

The fixed eight-role set, strict run schemas, deterministic context compiler, conditional token auditor, sixteen-family eval harness, role-aware tool gateway, Claude/OpenAI/Codex CLI adapter boundary, risk-tiered council engine, evidence-gated tuning policy, diff-bound publication gate, attestation-aware promotion definitions, and rollback workflow are implemented locally and tested. These controls do not by themselves prove a successful live provider run or deployment.

## Milestone sequence status

| Increment | State | Evidence boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Milestone 1 — contracts and governance | Implemented locally | ADR-0017, fixed manifest, source hashes, validator, tests, CI command |
| PR-A — telemetry foundation | Implemented locally | Runtime/JSON schemas, normalizers, redaction, sinks, CLI, deterministic tests |
| PR-B through PR-I | Implemented locally | Context, eval, policy, provider, council, tuning, publication, provenance, and rollback contracts/tests |
| PR-J — completion audit/freeze | In progress | Local audit passes; eight real live/external evidence gates remain open |

## Simulated orchestration boundary

The orchestration module remains a simulation for the business broker. The engineering-agent platform now has credential-gated HTTP adapters and a read-only ephemeral Codex CLI transport for controlled evals, but no persistent worker or autonomous production executor. Provider transports have no deployment authority.

## Authorized Phase 1.5 scope

- machine-readable role contracts and deterministic agent CI;
- automatic metadata-only run, token, context, cache, latency, retry, routing, and quality telemetry;
- bounded context selection and canonical provider-neutral prompt compilation;
- explainable provider-routing benchmarks and failure/capacity handoff;
- deterministic pre-tool allow, ask, or deny policy;
- functional, security, handoff, failure, and regression eval fixtures;
- correlated agent, quality, artifact, deployment, verification, approval, and rollback evidence.

Provider-native caching may be used and measured. Embeddings, vector storage, full RAG, graph indexing, semantic caching, and learned routing remain reserved extension points, not Phase 1.5 implementation work.

## Completion boundary

Phase 1.5 completes only when every gate in ADR-0017 and the completion audit has executable evidence. Current status is **in progress**, not frozen. See the [Phase 1.5 completion audit](/docs/plans/phase-1-5-completion-audit/) for the exact remaining external gates.

The supplied Tier 1 sources still define a broader brokered company with durable business work units, isolated execution, provider invocation, persistent audit, majority convergence, and human approvals. Those capabilities remain target state unless a current page, implementation, and test prove otherwise.
